  "term": "sleep–wake cycle",
  "definition": "The sleep–wake cycle is the usual 24-hour pattern of sleeping and being awake. When this pattern is disrupted, such as by travel, shift work, or other causes, it can be associated with circadian rhythm sleep disorders.",
